          <attvalue for="34" value="0.7" />
          <attvalue for="35" value="A spike in hostile or disruptive maritime incidents leads governments to treat shipping- and port-related data as a national-security asset and rapidly tighten legal and contractual limits on cross-border data sharing (especially with rival-state firms), increasing formal and de facto data-access restrictions." />
